  Junction reference artefacts (build123d/tests/test_underware_junctions.py):
  CGAL keeps touching volumes, so grip bases, each arm's junction-end cap, the
  T stem halves' and the corner quadrants' clip faces and the corners'
  path_extrude2d mitre joints are internal faces. At Added_Radius=0 (l.stl,
  l-y3-cutouts.stl) the L corner's outer wall is HOLLOW above z=9.905 over two
  ~22 degree bands (winding number 0 inside the 2 mm wall; 333 mm3 of the 8.67
  vs 9.00 cm3 pin spread): path_extrude2d sizes its mitre and joint-fill cubes
  from the path bounds (BOSL2 miscellaneous.scad:121-123, s = sqrt(2)*(r+0.81)
  = 19.81 mm here, so the section beyond s/2 of the centreline or above z = s/2
  stays unmitred); wide T corners' inside posts facet by up to 0.06 mm the
  same way. The 456fcd8 render and every Added_Radius >= 1 render at
  b86a7584 carry the solid wall; the port builds it solid.

