Text label deviations (build123d/holders/underware_text_label.py header):
- 0.4 mm 45 degree chamfer on every bed-face edge (bed-contact chamfers never
  yield, design-guidelines 8); parity compares the plate before it and pins
  the analytic reduction c^2/2 * perimeter - 4c^3/3.
- Text: Inter Bold via build123d/labels/label_text.py at OpenSCAD's em
  (1/0.72), strokes >= the labels inlay floor 0.7 mm; text_style inlaid
  (author default Text_Emboss=false: a two-colour flush inlay, like
  holders/label_card.py) or debossed (Text_Emboss=true). Default depth 0.6
  (labels INLAY_DEPTH), not 0.2. No Text_x_coordinate, fonts or colours.
- Not ported: Grip_Flare, Grip_Increase_Clearance, Suppress_Connectors,
  Decorative. Length stops at 11 units (bed), as for the I channel.
Published exceptions: the I channel's grip-end-wedge (every grip) and, for
debossed text, label-recess.

